A||N||11||reddog||sparks visible????||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||10-25-2001||11:28 PM||||Prettry sure I already know the answer to this one but I figured I would see if anyone else has this problem. When I open the engine compartment at night I notice that there is a small blue spark coming from a couple of the plug wires in the well where the boot meets the plug. I will press them on tight and you can't see the arc anymore. However, after a short drive I will look in the engine compartment again and see the same thing! Is this normal or do I need new wires? I just replaced them with allied signal wires a few months ago. What gives?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||California Kid||10-25-2001||11:58 PM||||Ignition wires are leaking, replace with real good ones.||||reg||1
Z||000002||reddog||10-26-2001||12:06 AM||||What are the BEST wires to use?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||California Kid||10-26-2001||01:09 AM||||I can only speak for myself, I'm using MSD Super Conductor high performance wires (got them thru Summit). They are 5 years old and still don't leak. Don't know if they offer a set for a V6, you may have to buy set for V8.<BR>They aren't cheap, but they are great.<P>Just a note for anyone else reading this, if you have a MSD Unit and coil over 45,000 volts, even premium wires will build resistance rather quickly. The MSD Unit tends to kick the hell out of the wires quickly. Was told that the wires should be replaced at about 10,000 miles for good performance (possibly earlier in some applications, you can check resistance of the wires with an omh meter). I know I'm over due, new wires in spring!!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Signature_7.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Oreif||10-26-2001||08:24 AM||||A decent performance wire set would be better. I use Accel 8.8mm wires. MSD and Moroso make very good wires too. Get at least 8mm wires. <P>------------------<BR>            <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/LOGO3.jpg">          <BR><FONT SIZE="1"><B><I>Happiness isn't around the corner...<BR>Happiness IS the corner.</I></B></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000005||theogre||10-26-2001||04:00 PM||||The wires are shot. Replace them. You're lucky you don't have a nasty skip to go with the arcing.<P>I'll stay with <A HREF="http://www.magnecor.com/" TARGET=_blank>Magnecor</A> myself. I've used them before but I didn't have the extra cash to put them on last time I needed wires when I bought my fiero.<P>For the price tho, about $25, the BWD (Borg Warner) wires I have now have held up amazingly well. They are at least a couple years old, a bit beat up, and still work ok. there's no arc overs or any of that crap. And this is a DIS motor. DIS pumps out way more power than HEI.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">  <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000006||Fiero_Freak||10-26-2001||06:19 PM||||  Ditto on the MSD's.  I bought a set.. for a few extra bucks worth of connectors you can make yourself another set.  I bought the universal v8 with multi-angle TPI type boots.  It was accually cheaper and I have two sets worth...plus some extra wire.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Fiero_Left_01.jpg"> <BR>Two '87 GT's...<BR>   ...Double Trouble||||reg||1
Z||000007||reddog||10-26-2001||06:45 PM||||Well I went ahead and bought a set of the Accel 8mm Hi pro wires. Also blew some money on a Accel control module and a super coil. I didn't know too much about them.Have seen mixed reviews of the product . What the heck I figured I would give it a whirl.. Will put them on tommorrow!<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Smoooooth GT||10-26-2001||11:30 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by reddog:<BR><B>Well I went ahead and bought a set of the Accel 8mm Hi pro wires. Also blew some money on a Accel control module and a super coil. I didn't know too much about them.Have seen mixed reviews of the product . What the heck I figured I would give it a whirl.. Will put them on tommorrow!<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE>good luck with the Accel super coil... mine lasted me only 6,500 miles or so...    Steve<P><P>------------------<BR>NOS Injected 2.8L V/6<BR>UNDER CONSTRUCTION   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/smooth_sig2_4_1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000009||rodmcneill||10-27-2001||01:48 AM||||You may also want to check your spark plugs for excessive gap-worn out. The distributor cap and rotor are also prone to internal corrosion.||||reg||1
Z||000010||Seanh||10-27-2001||05:49 PM||||I'v never had a problem with my Accel coil yet, but my engine eats Accel modules for lunch, atleast a new one every 2 months, maybe the AC delco one will last longer this time...||||reg||1
Z||000011||reddog||11-01-2001||10:54 PM||||Well, everybody can go ahead and tell me "I told you so", I put the Accel control module on and it worked pretty good for about 10 miles! I got on the throttle a little and all of the sudden it died .It just quit in the middle of deccelaration immediately followed by a huge Backfire. Called Fiero Store and they said that failure doesn't usually happen with the module "WHATEVER" does any other company make an aftermarket performance module like the accel, That acually works?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Cutout_1.gif"> ||||reg||1
